course: dictionary
lesson: 13626
title: Words that mean cannot be told apart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indistinguishable is a long word, but you can break it into parts. In- means not, distinguish means tell apart, and -able means can be. So indistinguishable means cannot be told apart.
explain: «The twins wore the same clothes, and their faces were indistinguishable.» Nobody could tell which twin was which. Two things are indistinguishable when they look, sound or feel so alike that you cannot find a difference.
explain: The word can also mean so faint or unclear that you cannot pick something out. «In the thick fog, the hill was indistinguishable from the grey sky.» You could not see where one stopped and the other began. Phrases like «almost indistinguishable» and «virtually indistinguishable» mean nearly the same.
fact: Indistinguishable means so alike that you cannot tell them apart.
fact: «The two liquids were indistinguishable, so the scientist ran a test to find the difference.»
fact: «Some poisonous berries look indistinguishable from safe ones, so never eat a berry you do not know.»
fact: In maths, indistinguishable objects are objects you count as the same, such as identical balls.
fact: Useful phrases: «indistinguishable from», «almost indistinguishable», «virtually indistinguishable».
exercise: «The two coins were indistinguishable in the dark.» What does indistinguishable mean? | Brand new and shiny | Very loud and clear | Heavy and cold | *So alike that you cannot tell them apart
exercise: «Her copy was almost indistinguishable from the real painting.» What does almost indistinguishable suggest? | *The copy looks nearly the same as the real painting | The copy is wet and muddy | The real painting was lost | The copy is much bigger than the painting
exercise: «In the fog, the hill was ___ from the sky.» Which word fits the gap? | delicious | sparkling | *indistinguishable | enormous
test: «The twins looked indistinguishable, so even their teacher was confused.» What does indistinguishable mean here? | Very tall and thin | Loud and happy | Easy to tell apart | *So alike that they cannot be told apart
test: Why might a safety sign warn about berries that look indistinguishable from safe ones? | To say they taste sweet | To say they are the same colour as the grass | *Because dangerous berries can look the same as safe ones | To say they are very big
exam: Which word means so alike that you cannot tell them apart? | banana | *indistinguishable | quickly | purple
